cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AADAGE (Automorphism Aware Directed Attributed Graph Explorer)
message: >-
  If you use AADAGE, please cite the reference article describing the
  method, and/or this software.
type: software
authors:
  - affiliation: I3S Laboratory, CNRS, Université Côte d'Azur
    email: claude.pasquier@univ-cotedazur.fr
    family-names: Pasquier
    given-names: Claude
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2012-12-01"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/claudepasquier/aadage"
keywords:
  - graph mining
  - attributed graphs
  - frequent pattern mining
  - automorphism
  - itemset mining
abstract: >-
  AADAGE extracts frequent patterns from one or more directed attributed
  graphs, i.e. graphs in which nodes are associated with sets of attributes.
  It reduces the combinatorial explosion induced by subgraph isomorphisms
  thanks to an appropriate processing of automorphic patterns.
